7592186536934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186536950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186536954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186536972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1045 "The Multivariable Chain Rule in Vector Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186536972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536279 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a420db12-a105-5bd9-937a-e05193194ef3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536909 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536950 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536909 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1d9d61a2-d905-5297-b0d3-ec95675b960d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536909 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536934 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "664e440a-aede-58bf-9a8e-056fd99ee996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536934 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536950 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536950 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8aab6ae2-020e-5223-9fc4-3a53a2218b2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536950 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536954 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536954 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "97d5963d-f21c-5cdb-abef-05d8b1a46545" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536954 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186360526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536972 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186536954 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536972 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d8cbd27c-a659-536b-a17d-a2d28ebe3156" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186536972 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186479902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542514 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542551 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542514 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542514 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)=3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t,3,\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩$ at the point $t=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542514 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "034848a3-a1f9-5d8f-b396-bccbb706e96e" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542514 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 z^{2},- 9 y^{2},6 x z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t$, $y=3$, $z=\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨3 \\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)^{2},- 9 \\cdot 3^{2},6 \\left(- 3 t\\right) \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(3 t^{2} - 9\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(-81\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)+\\left(- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}\\right) \\\\  & =- 9 t^{2} + 27+0- 18 t^{2} \\\\  & =- 27 t^{2} + 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(2))] & =- 27 (2)^{2} + 27 \\\\  & =-9+0-72 \\\\  & =-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542527 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542519 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542527 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542527 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨t,- 3 t + 1⟩$ at the point $t=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542527 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "53b4c038-e54a-5606-9304-0b269648dd21" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542527 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2} - 2 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x^{2} - 2 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 x,- 4 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=t$, $y=- 3 t + 1$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨2 t,- 4 \\left(- 3 t + 1\\right)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 t,12 t - 4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t + 1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨2 t,12 t - 4⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(2 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)+\\left(12 t - 4\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right) \\\\  & =- 34 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(1))] & =- 34 (1) + 12 \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542538 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542543 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542538 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542538 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y)=- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- t + 2,2 t⟩$ at the point $t=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542538 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9dcc91d6-8511-52d2-b88b-562fac2dd7c9" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542538 #edb/ref 1074 "The rate of change of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 3 x^{2} + 3 y^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 6 x,6 y⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- t + 2$, $y=2 t$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨- 6 \\left(- t + 2\\right),6 \\cdot 2 t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6 t - 12,12 t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- t + 2),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨6 t - 12,12 t⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(6 t - 12\\right)\\cdot \\left(-1\\right)+\\left(12 t\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\  & =18 t + 12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begi